Subject: [PATCH] /start: make Kodarai understandable to beginners; update
 questionnaire

- Plain-English strip under hero (problem / what Kodarai does / what you do)
- Illustrative worked example (clearly labelled, not a real customer)
- Rewrite how-it-works steps in plain language
- FAQ: coding, contacting owners, pricing, rejection, no income guarantee
- Hero: three plain-language headlines that rotate with a fade/slide (same
  motion as the landing hero), led by 'Earn money building websites for
  businesses that don't have one, local or abroad.'; stacked in one grid cell
  so nothing shifts; respects prefers-reduced-motion; /start?h=earn|client|find
  pins one headline for A/B tests and fires start_hook_viewed
- Remove remaining 'free / no credit card' claims (result page, final CTA);
  prices read from billing helpers instead of hardcoded
- Questionnaire: plainer wording, add 50,000 NGN goal option, 'complete
  beginner' option, 'Businesses don't reply to me'
